.TH NETSTATPLUS 1 "November 2026" "Custom Shell" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
netstatplus \- extended network connection monitor with real-time traffic analysis
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B netstatplus
[\fIoptions\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B netstatplus
reads the kernel's network socket tables from
.I /proc/net/tcp
,
.I /proc/net/tcp6
,
.I /proc/net/udp
,
and
.I /proc/net/udp6
to display active connections with their state, local and remote addresses,
and ports.
Unlike traditional \fBnetstat\fR(8),
.B netstatplus
provides continuous real-time monitoring using \fBpoll()\fR(2) to observe
transfer rates (bytes per second) over a configurable interval without busy-waiting.
Between each snapshot the command computes deltas from the previous observation,
displaying approximate throughput for every connection.

Interrupts (\fBSIGINT\fR or \fBSIGTERM\fR) cause a graceful exit after the
current iteration finishes displaying data.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-t
Show only TCP connections (the default when no protocol flag is given).
.TP
.B \-u
Show only UDP connections.
.TP
.B \-l
Show only listening sockets (\fBST\f state).
.TP
.B \-n
Display numeric addresses and ports; skip name resolution.
.TP
.BI \-i " SECONDS"
Update interval in seconds (default: 1.0). The value must be greater than 0.
Fractional values are supported (e.g. \fB\-i 0.5\fR for half-second updates).
.TP
.B \-1
One-shot mode: display a single snapshot and exit immediately instead of looping.
.TP
.B \-h
Print usage information and exit with status 0.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success; all connections listed without error.
.TP
.B 1
An internal or system error occurred (could not open \fI/proc\fR files, read
failure, etc.).
.TP
.B 2
Usage error: an invalid option or combination of options was supplied.
.TP
.B 130
The process was interrupted by \fBSIGINT\fR (Ctrl-C).
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Show all active TCP connections with live traffic rates:
.RS
.nf
$ netstatplus \-t
  Proto  Recv\-Q Send\-Q Local Address          Foreign Address        State         RX        TX
  tcp    0      0      192\.168\.1\.10:443      10\.45\.67\.89:52340     ESTABLISHED   12.4 KB/s  8.7 KB/s
  tcp    0      0      192\.168\.1\.10:80       172\.16\.0\.5:48812     ESTABLISHED   3\.1 MB/s   1.2 MB/s
  tcp    0      0      0\.0\.0\.0:22            0\.0\.0\.0:*             LISTEN        0 B/s     0 B/s
.fi
.RE
.PP
List only listening UDP sockets in numeric mode:
.RS
.nf
$ netstatplus \-u \-l \-n
  Proto  Recv\-Q Send\-Q Local Address          Foreign Address        State         RX        TX
  udp    0      0      0\.0\.0\.0:68            0\.0\.0\.0:*             LISTEN        0 B/s     0 B/s
.fi
.RE
.PP
One-shot display of all connections:
.RS
.nf
$ netstatplus \-1
.fi
.RE
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /proc/net/tcp
TCPv4 socket table.
.TP
.I /proc/net/tcp6
TCPv6 socket table.
.TP
.I /proc/net/udp
UDPv4 socket table.
.TP
.I /proc/net/udp6
UDPv6 socket table.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR netstat (8),
.BR poll (2),
.BR proc (5)
